mple, if `decimals` equals `2`, a balance of `505` tokens should be displayed to a user as `5.05` (`505 / 10 ** 2`). Tokens usually opt for a value of 18, imitating the relationship between Ether and Wei. This is the value {ERC20} uses, unless this function is overridden; NOTE: This information is only used for _display_ purposes: it in no way affects any of the arithmetic of the contract, including {IERC20-balanceOf} and {IERC20-transfer}."},"decreaseAllowance(address,uint256)":{"details":"Atomically decreases the allowance granted to `spender` by the caller. This is an alternative to {approve} that can be used as a mitigation for problems described in {IERC20-approve}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address. - `spender` must have allowance for the caller of at least `subtractedValue`."},"find(uint256,uint256,uint256,address)":{"details":"Find the dices of the target address (in reverse order)","params":{"count":"Maximum number of records returned","maxFindCount":"Find records at most","owner":"Target address","start":"Find forward from the index corresponding to the given contract address  (excluding the record corresponding to start)"},"returns":{"diceArray":"Matched dice array"}},"getDiceCount()":{"details":"Obtain the number of dices that have been opened","returns":{"_0":"Number of dices opened"}},"increaseAllowance(address,uint256)":{"details":"Atomically increases the allowance granted to `spender` by the caller. This is an alternative to {approve} that can be used as a mitigation for problems described in {IERC20-approve}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. Requirements: - `spender` cannot be the zero address."},"initialize(address)":{"details":"To support open-zeppelin/upgrades","params":{"governance":"IHedgeGovernance implementation contract address"}},"list(uint256,uint256,uint256)":{"details":"List dice","params":{"count":"Return (count) records","offset":"Skip previous (offset) records","order":"Order. 0 reverse order, non-0 positive order"},"returns":{"diceArray":"Matched dice array"}},"mint(address,uint256)":{"details":"Mint FortRPC","params":{"to":"Target address","value":"Mint amount"}},"name()":{"details":"Returns the name of the token."},"roll(uint256,uint256)":{"details":"start a roll dice","params":{"m":"times, 4 decimals","n":"count of PRC"}},"setMinter(address,uint256)":{"details":"Set mining permission flag","params":{"account":"Target address","flag":"Mining permission flag"}},"symbol()":{"details":"Returns the symbol of the token, usually a shorter version of the name."},"totalSupply()":{"details":"See {IERC20-totalSupply}."},"transfer(address,uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC20-transfer}. Requirements: - `to` cannot be the zero address. - the caller must have a balance of at least `amount`."},"transferFrom(address,address,uint256)":{"details":"See {IERC20-transferFrom}. Emits an {Approval} event indicating the updated allowance. This is not required by the EIP. See the note at the beginning of {ERC20}. NOTE: Does not update the allowance if the current allowance is the maximum `uint256`. Requirements: - `from` and `to` cannot be the zero address. - `from` must have a balance of at least `amount`. - the caller must have allowance for ``from``'s tokens of at least `amount`."},"update(address)":{"details":"Rewritten in the implementation contract, for load other contract addresses. Call       super.update(newGovernance) when overriding, and override method without onlyGovernance","params":{"newGovernance":"IHedgeGovernance implementation contract address"}}},"version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{},"version":1}},"settings":{"compilationTarget":{"FortPRC.sol":"FortPRC"},"evmVersion":"london","libraries":{},"metadata":{"bytecodeHash":"ipfs"},"optimizer":{"enabled":true,"runs":888888},"remappings":[]},"sources":{"FortPRC.sol":{"keccak256":"0x5344b761361c2b751a3d020cd6f0c9a6ce4bb09562f8d784957481c9560